NAME
       subscription-manager - register the system with Red Hat and manage its content

SYNOPSIS
       subscription-manager COMMAND [OPTIONS]

DESCRIPTION
       subscription-manager connects a RHEL system to Red Hat's customer
       portal (or a Satellite server). Once registered, the system receives
       Red Hat's package repositories, which dnf then uses.

       Practice and exam systems are usually not registered. They get their
       packages from local repositories instead: a repository server on the
       network, or the installation DVD, set up with .repo files in
       /etc/yum.repos.d.

COMMANDS
       status Show whether the system is registered and has access to
              content.

       register
              Register the system with a user name and password or an
              activation key.

       repos --list
              List the repositories available through the subscription.

       unregister
              Remove the registration.

EXAMPLES
           subscription-manager status

SEE ALSO
       dnf(8), yum.conf(5)
